urname>Lindner</surname><given-names>KH</given-names></name><name><surname>Rockemann</surname><given-names>MG</given-names></name><name><surname>Schirmer</surname><given-names>U</given-names></name><name><surname>Schwilk</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Effect of 7.2% hypertonic saline/6% hetastarch on left ventricular contractility in anesthetized humans</article-title><source>Anesthesiology</source><year>1995</year><volume>82</volume><fpage>1389</fpage><lpage>95</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7540812</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b16-21-re-0010"><label>16</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Oliveira</surname><given-names>SA</given-names></name><name><surname>Bueno</surname><given-names>RM</given-names></name><name><surname>Souza</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name><name><surname>Senra</surname><given-names>DF</given-names></name><name><surname>Rocha-e-Silva</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Effects of hypertonic saline dextran on the postoperative evolution of Jehovah&#x02019;s Witness patients submitted to cardiac surgery with cardiopulmonary bypass</article-title><source>Shock</source><year>1995</year><volume>3</volume><fpage>391</fpage><lpage>4</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7544684</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b17-21-re-0010"><label>17</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Christ</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Niklas</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Kreimeier</surname><given-names>U</given-names></name><name><surname>Lauterjung</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Peter</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Messmer</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Hyperosmotic-hyperoncotic solutions during abdomin